B.JV=new A.bi(B.eH,["RT-TEC: Real-Time Trade Eligibility Classifier","Sub-10ms ML system for real-time trade decisions","assets/images/RT_TEC.png","Developed a production-grade, real-time trading decision system using FastAPI and NVIDIA Triton for GPU-accelerated ML inference. The system determines trade eligibility in milliseconds, ensuring compliance and safety in high-frequency trading environments.","Key features include sub-10ms latency, fail-safe design, multi-layer validation, and comprehensive audit trails using PostgreSQL. The architecture incorporates Feast and Redis for real-time feature serving, RedPanda for market data ingestion, and Prometheus with Grafana for monitoring. The system supports hot-swappable models, A/B testing, and version management, making it ideal for high-frequency trading firms and algorithmic trading platforms.",B.I0,"https://github.com/Aashay7/RT-TEC","Personal Project / Lead Developer","Jul 2025 - Present","In Progress"],t.yf)
B.Hb=s(["RAG","FastAPI","SQLite","Embeddings","Summarization","Document QA","NLP"],t.s)
B.JS=new A.bi(B.eH,["Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) for Finance Applications","Local prototype for document QA and summarization","images/RAGFinance.png","Built a local prototype of a Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) system for financial documents using FastAPI and SQLite. The system supports document ingestion, chunking, embedding, retrieval, and summarization, enabling users to ask questions and get concise answers from a corpus of financial texts.","The pipeline includes a demo document ingestion endpoint, recent document listing, and a question-answering interface that retrieves relevant chunks and generates summaries. The system uses sentence-transformers for embeddings and can leverage OpenAI\u2019s API for advanced summarization if an API key is provided. This project showcases the potential of RAG in financial applications, providing a foundation for more complex deployments.",B.Hb,"https://github.com/Aashay7/rag-finance","Personal Project / Lead Developer","Aug 2025 - Present","In Progress"],t.yf)
B.HS=s(["NeRF","3D Reconstruction","TensorFlow","PyTorch","Slurm","NumPy"],t.s)
B.JU=new A.bi(B.eH,["3D View Synthesis using NeRF","Neural Radiance Fields for novel view generation","assets/images/NeRFCVPoster.jpeg","Implemented 3D scene reconstruction using volumetric rendering and ray sampling techniques, based on the NeRF paper (https://arxiv.org/abs/2003.08934). Final training on IU\u2019s Carbonate GPU cluster using TensorFlow. Used both PyTorch and TF for experimentation.","This project involved creating a neural network that can generate novel views of a scene from a sparse set of input images. The model learns to represent the scene as a continuous volumetric field, allowing it to synthesize new perspectives by sampling rays through the volume. The implementation was optimized for performance and accuracy, leveraging advanced techniques like positional encoding and hierarchical sampling.",B.HS,"https://github.com/Aashay7/NERF_","Lead Developer","Jan 2022 - May 2022","Completed"],t.yf)
B.KL={title:0,description:1,image:2,details:3,additionalDetails:4,tags:5,link:6,role:7,duration:8,status:9,published:10}
B.Ib=s(["assets/images/IoTHM/IoTHM_1.png","assets/images/IoTHM/IoTHM_2.png","assets/images/IoTHM/IoTHM_3.png","assets/images/IoTHM/IoTHM_4.png","assets/images/IoTHM/IoTHM_5.png"],t.s)
B.I8=s(["IoT","Wearables","Time Series","Anomaly Detection","Arduino","Sensors","Python"],t.s)
B.JX=new A.bi(B.KL,["IoT Health Monitor for Rescue Teams","Health tracking system with ML insights",B.Ib,"Monitored vitals like heartbeat, humidity, and temperature using wearable IoT. ML models used for real-time health predictions of rescue teams. Project focused on deployment stability and sensor accuracy.","Designed a low-power wearable stack (microcontroller + sensors) streaming via BLE/Wi-Fi to a gateway. Implemented feature engineering on time-series vitals, anomaly detection for fatigue/heat stress, and alert thresholds. Emphasis on robustness, calibration, and false-positive control in field conditions.",B.I8,"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1877050918310202","Student / Researcher","Jan 2018 - Apr 2018","Completed","2018 - International Conference on Robotics and Smart Manufacturing (RoSMa2018)"],t.yf)
B.Hp=s(["Flutter","BioBERT","Transformer","QuestionAnswering","TensorFlow","Medical NLP","FAISS","DocProduct"],t.s)
B.JR=new A.bi(B.eH,["Flutter App: Chatbot powered by BioBERT","Biomedical Q&A chatbot with BioBERT retrieval and answer generation backend; Flutter client for a clean mobile UX.","https://source.unsplash.com/400x300/?medical,ai","Built a medical Q&A chatbot where a Flutter app talks to a TensorFlow 2.0 backend that fine-tunes BioBERT for dense retrieval and uses lightweight heads for similarity search. The service ranks top passages and (optionally) conditions a small generative head for natural, readable answers. Architecture inspired by DocProduct.","Data pipeline for PubMed/QA sources (cleaning, tokenization via WordPiece, truncation with sliding windows, attention masks). Fine-tuned BioBERT embeddings with twin FCNN heads for question/answer metric learning; FAISS-style nearest-neighbor retrieval; optional GPT-style rephrasing. Exposed REST endpoints consumed by Flutter; handled OOV, max_seq_len (512), batching, and beam-style reranking. Evaluated with retrieval@k, EM/F1 (SQuAD-style), and expert spot-checks for clinical coherence and safety disclaimers.",B.Hp,"https://github.com/Aashay7/BERT/blob/master/DocProductPresentationV6_0_2_0.ipynb","NLP Engineer","Jul 2017 - Dec 2017","Completed"],t.yf)
B.KX={title:0,description:1,details:2,additionalDetails:3,image:4,tags:5,link:6,role:7,duration:8,status:9,published:10}
B.GX=s(["Computer Vision","BRISK","Haar Cascade","Feature Matching","OpenCV","RANSAC"],t.s)
B.Kd=new A.bi(B.KX,["Face Recognition (BRISK + Haar Cascading)","Best CS Project @ VIT 2017\u201318","Combined BRISK descriptors with Haar Cascading for real-time face verification. Honored as best project from VIT CSE, presented at ICMCE 2017. Featured strong preprocessing and outlier rejection.","Used Haar Cascade as a robust detector, then BRISK keypoints + binary descriptor matching with ratio tests to verify identity. Tuned inlier thresholds and RANSAC filtering for robustness under illumination/pose changes; profiled for real-time constraints.","",B.GX,"https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/abstract/document/9077901/","Computer Vision Researcher","Jul 2017 - Dec 2017","Awarded / Completed","2020 International Conference on Emerging Trends in Information Technology and Engineering (ic-ETITE)"],t.yf)
B.tX={title:0,description:1,image:2,details:3,additionalDetails:4,tags:5,role:6,duration:7,status:8}
B.Hl=s(["Ethereum","Solidity","Truffle","Web3","dApp","Smart Contracts","MetaMask"],t.s)
B.JP=new A.bi(B.tX,["Distributed Farmers Market (Blockchain)","Ethereum dApp using Truffle framework","https://source.unsplash.com/400x300/?blockchain,crypto","Built a decentralized transparent marketplace for farmers using Ethereum and the Truffle framework. Included buyer/seller contract logic, wallet auth, and item listing on the blockchain.","Wrote Solidity smart contracts for listing, escrow, and fulfillment; integrated Web3 wallet auth (MetaMask) and event-driven UI. Implemented Truffle migrations, Ganache local testing, and basic gas optimizations. Frontend stack used modular JS with a clean, minimal UI.",B.Hl,"Full-stack Developer","Jul 2017 - Dec 2017","Completed"],t.yf)
B.Ho=s(["IoT","Arduino","Accelerometer","Signal Processing","Anomaly Detection","Twitter API"],t.s)
B.JQ=new A.bi(B.tX,["Earthquake Detection with Twitter Alerts","IoT sensors + automated earthquake reporting","https://source.unsplash.com/400x300/?earthquake,alert","Arduino-based motion sensors used to detect seismic activity. Triggered automated Twitter alerts using Ethernet modules. Calibrated accelerometer for noise filtering and false positive reduction.","Calibrated accelerometer bias/drift; implemented band-pass filtering and dynamic thresholds to detect seismic-like patterns. On trigger, posted alerts via API with rate-limit safeguards. Focused on latency, reliability, and low-power behavior.",B.Ho,"Embedded Engineer","Jul 2017 - Dec 2017","Completed"],t.yf)
B.HP=s(["OCR","Recommender Systems","KMeans","Scrapy","NLP","TF-IDF","Fuzzy Matching"],t.s)
B.JT=new A.bi(B.eH,["OCR Book Recommender","Goodreads + OCR + KMeans clustering","https://source.unsplash.com/400x300/?books,ml","Built an OCR-based book scanner that fetches metadata from Goodreads and recommends similar books using KMeans. Integrated a Scrapy-based web crawler and a fuzzy-matching title resolver.","Used OCR preprocessing (binarization, deskew, denoise) and text cleanup; crawled metadata and reviews, engineered TF-IDF/embeddings, and clustered with KMeans to suggest similar titles. Added rule-based tie-breakers on ratings/genres for better UX.",B.HP,null,"Data Scientist","Jul 2017 - Dec 2017","Completed"],t.yf)
